course: dictionary
lesson: 1743
title: Clapping: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Clapping means hitting your hands together again and again to make a sound, to show you liked something or to cheer. Look at the words around it: «Cartoons show a dolphin always smiling and a seal clapping and balancing a ball». The clapping seal is a trained sea lion, so the word describes a performer's act, not a wild animal's.
explain: Clapping can also mean a sudden loud noise like thunder, or a friendly pat. The clues tell you which: thunder is loud and sudden, and in «clapping him on the back», the words him and back show that it is a pat, not a sound.
explain: Clapping is the -ing form of «clap», so you will also see clap, claps and clapped. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If «clapping» means a friendly pat and the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Clapping is a noun you do not count, so you say «clapping», not «a clapping».
fact: Clapping means hitting your hands together to make a sound, to show praise or to cheer.
fact: In music lessons, clapping helps you feel the beat: «Picture a class clapping "ta, ta, ti-ti, ta"».
fact: Rhythm is the pattern of beats in a line, made by strong and weak syllables, and clapping helps you feel it.
fact: Clapping games like «Miss Mary Mack» and «A sailor went to sea» are playground rhymes.
exercise: At the end of the assembly the whole hall starts clapping. What does the clapping show? | *Thanks and praise | A cold wind | Anger at a late start | Sleepiness
exercise: «clapping him on the back» is a friendly action. What does clapping mean here? | *A friendly pat | Hitting someone hard to make them fall | A loud crash like thunder | Counting the beats of a song
exercise: «Thunder came clapping over the hills.» Which meaning of clapping fits best? | Dancing slowly | Hitting hands together to cheer | *A sudden loud noise | Patting a friend
test: In «a class clapping "ta, ta, ti-ti, ta"», what are the children practising? | *Keeping the beat of a rhythm | Hiding from the teacher | Writing a story | Choosing a seal for a cartoon
test: Which sentence uses clapping correctly as a noun you do not count? | I heard many clappings from the hall | I heard three clappings from the hall | *I heard clapping from the hall | I heard a clapping from the hall
exam: Read «Rhythm is the pattern of beats in a line, made by strong and weak syllables; clapping helps you feel it.» What is clapping helping you do? | Forget the weak syllables | Spell the strong syllables | *Feel the pattern of beats | Make the lines longer
